 "decision": "Direct-load dp4a Q5_K schedule REJECTED at the leaf: loses to the retained raw mmq32 owner on every actual weight screened (geomean raw/direct 0.64x at R32, 0.72x at R24 over 6 weights x 5 samples, alternating order, operation-complete incl. quantize). Correctness vs the raw owner is clean (KL 4.5e-15 on blk.0 R32; max_rel entries with large magnitude are near-zero-denominator artifacts, abs diff max 6.7e-6). Two variants measured: per-thread scale recompute (best, this artifact) and a pack-lane __shfl_up scale broadcast (slower, 0.537x R32). Root cause per the iter37 inspection class: the raw GGUF Q5_K layout has no record structure permitting coalesced direct loads - each thread reads 8 columns at 4224 B stride (uncoalesced sectors), which is why the retained owners stage through LDS and why the source-layout owner exists. The mechanism-backed remaining axis is a Q5 analogue of the proven T16 qmicro-planar repack + dp4a kernel family (the schedule that reaches 101-134 GB/s on this regime).",
